# mergerfs pool configuration (sourced by start-pool.sh)

# Where the merged pool appears. Point Samba/file manager here.
MOUNTPOINT="/DATA/Storage"

# Colon-separated branches = the ZimaOS-managed DATA disks to pool.
# IMPORTANT: do NOT include the SnapRAID parity disk here.
# ZimaOS mounts data disks under /media/sdX (also bind-mirrored to /DATA/.media/).
# Example two disks:
BRANCHES="/media/sda:/media/sdb"

# At boot, start-pool.sh waits up to this many seconds for EVERY branch above to be
# mounted by the ZimaOS storage daemon before launching mergerfs (the primary fix for
# the pool-vs-storage boot race). Raise it if your disks spin up slowly. Default: 90.
#BRANCH_WAIT=90

# mergerfs options (proven baseline from the PoC + safe additions).
#  - category.create=mfs       : write new files to the disk with most free space
#  - minfreespace=20G          : keep 20G headroom per branch
#  - moveonenospc=true         : move file to another branch if a disk fills mid-write
#  - branches-mount-timeout=30 : at boot, wait up to 30s for the ZimaOS automounts
#                                (/media/sdX) before giving up — mitigates the
#                                pool-vs-storage ordering race. mergerfs >=2.40.
#  - allow_other + default_permissions : allow_other exposes the pool to ALL local
#    users (needed for Samba etc.) — so the UNDERLYING disk permissions become the
#    only access control. default_permissions makes the kernel ENFORCE those modes
#    on every access. Keep both, or drop allow_other if only root needs the pool.
# FUSE passthrough: this ZimaOS kernel has CONFIG_FUSE_PASSTHROUGH=y. mergerfs
# >=2.41 supports it — enable only after confirming the exact option name/values
# against the 2.42.0 docs, then add it here. Not enabled by default.
OPTS="defaults,allow_other,default_permissions,cache.files=partial,dropcacheonclose=true,category.create=mfs,minfreespace=20G,moveonenospc=true,branches-mount-timeout=30"
